A||N||6||kornholio||removing steering wheel||||1||
Z||000000||kornholio||03-11-2001||10:58 PM||||I have a Grant steering wheel that I need to remove and reposition.  How hard is it to do?  I can rent a steering wheel puller.  I just don't know how to use one.  And how do I get the wheel back on?  Is a wheel puller the only special tool I need?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||stsmithgt||03-12-2001||09:57 AM||||The steering wheel puller is cheap.  Well the one I bought was cheap.  I taped a small bearing on the end of the bolt that pushes on the steering shaft to make the cheap one work better.<BR>     That's <I>not</I> the only tool.  There's a tool to get the snap ring off.  That spring loaded plate is pushing up against it on the shaft.  If you push in that plate, you'll see the snap ring.  It's a PITA<B>!</B> to get off without it, but it's possible.  Be sure kids aren't around when you try without it.  Your vocabulary might get a little vulgure. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> #?¿¤%!*?#@%$^%||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||03-12-2001||10:03 AM||||Oh yeah,  I forgot to mention about those Grant steering wheel adaptors.  Mine was aluminum so I'll <I>assume</I> yours it too.  Torque that puppy down.  I'm not sure what the torque specs are because I didn't use them, but I thought I had mine tight and it kept coming loose.  I would start to feel the wheel click back and fourth with a little extra pressure.  Not good for aluminum.  Just something to look out for.  Mines fine now. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driversid1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||03-12-2001||11:05 AM||||I bought a puller one time from Pep Boys when I was visiting Buffalo.  Changed my steering wheel in the parking lot and then returned the puller 1/2 hour later.  It is easy to do and even if you keep the puller it's cheap.  Needless to say I drove over the boarder back to Toronto with a new wheel and didn't have to pay duty.  I had a puller at home but that was the problem, I wasn't at home and I didn't want to pay duty just because I wasn't in the U.S. for more than 24 hours.||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||03-12-2001||05:57 PM||||stsmithgt:  what kinda of shifter is that you have there?  is that for an auto or manual?||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||03-12-2001||06:08 PM||||That's a manual tranny 4spd. with a B&M shift handle drilled and tapped to fit. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000006||rogergarrison||03-12-2001||08:42 PM||||me and lisa just put her new steering wheel on. used a grant signature adapter, but the other one is same way. the horn switch comes thru the casting, so you cant move it except where its at, you need to center it with the tie rod ends. The steering wheel adapter will only go on in one position.||||reg||1
